WEBVTT

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.900
Now we don't have anything
to worry about, pyuru!

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.740
We can perform in the
Grateful Rock Festival! I'm so happy!

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.950
It's still too early to feel relieved.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.370
'Cause it's like we just
barely made it to the start line.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.910
Yes, that's true.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.330
Cyan!

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.960
I feel so lucky to be able to see you again!

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.380
That girl ignored me and went to Cyan...

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.680
After coming here, Cyan, your
popularity's gone through the roof, pyuru!

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.760
Everyone's talking about you online, too!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.010
What? That's not true.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.470
You all were good, too,
so it can't be just me...

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.190
I'm glad Plasmagica won.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.400
But, what is this feeling...?

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.240
Hm?

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.870
Her Melodisian has
evolved more than expected.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.750
Hm?

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:06.420
Oh, this is good.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.310
<i>Ready... 1, 2, 3, GO!</i>

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.140
<i>Love life! Very! Very! Happy!</i>

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.940
<i>Friendship life! Bouncing, jumping!</i>

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.650
<i>Adventure life! Heart-pounding, OK?</i>

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.610
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:36.240
<i>Rushing out onto the road to</i>
<i>school with the blue sky behind us</i>

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.200
<i>I like that! I like this, too!</i>

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.700
<i>I'll take it all, all of it~</i>

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.580
<i>A girl who imagines love is all romance</i>

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.330
<i>If I can attack, I'll do it boldly</i>

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.960
<i>Let's find an original vision for the future</i>

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.890
<i>Sometimes, we'll have a secret love advice time</i>

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.720
<i>Who do you like?</i>

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:08.270
<i>You've got a green light for love now!</i>
<i>It's your chance to move forward!</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.110
<i>So, let's just</i>

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.110
<i>Have a blast! Fall in love!</i>

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.190
<i>Our youth is non-stop!</i>

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.280
<i>Run! Aim for the future!</i>

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.910
<i>Everyone gather</i>

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.780
<i>For a happy ending!</i>

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.330
<i>Will tomorrow be happy or sad?</i>
<i>Will we idle our time away?</i>

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.410
<i>We'll work hard!</i>

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.710
<i>I want to keep dreaming forever!</i>

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.920
<i>Let's fly out into the</i>
<i>world with all our strength!</i>

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:36.800
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:46.560
"Cyan from Plasmagica draws even more
attention sharing lead vocals on their new song—

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:51.650
Looking forward to her performance
in the Grateful Rock Festival" huh?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:59.450
One day, I will stand at
the top of the music world.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.830
That is my goal. No, my ambition.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.460
In order to make that
come true, I will do anything.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.250
Even if it means using
my friends as stepping-stones.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.510
That's right. I won't hesitate.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.180
We finally defeated Criticrista,
who could be called our archenemies,

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.760
and are now in the spotlight.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.900
However, why is the spotlight not on me—

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:39.740
Oh?

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:42.700
She has a lot of ambition.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:46.240
But, I love girls like that...

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:58.220
♪ Falling star of dreams shining in the night sky ♪

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:58.550
That was fun... And we won, too.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.140
♪ I want to see it from the same place as you ♪

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.010
It was perfect!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.560
What's with your completely
relaxed face and attitude?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:07.770
♪ No matter how far apart we are ♪

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.310
Mr. Berry?! I missed you!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.100
Anyway, where have you been?

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.810
And I wanted your advice
about stuff before our concert, too...

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.190
Wait!

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.820
The small talk can wait.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.150
My business comes first!

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.280
R-Right.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.320
Get the other members here ASAP!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.740
Hm? Okay, I will...

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.630
First of all, congratulations on making
it into the Grateful Rock Festival.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.210
Thank you very much.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.420
Yeah, well, that's what
happens when we get serious.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.140
It's still too early to celebrate.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:51.180
You know that the hot and cool bands
of Midi City gather for the festival, right?

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.310
Yeah...

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.440
There's no doubt that Dagger will
plant dark monsters at the rock festival.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.320
His goal will be to attack the
popular bands gathered there.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:02.700
That's...

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.320
That's not all.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.910
He's probably also thinking of
taking advantage of the confusion,

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.370
and turning the Melodisians
of the audience into dark stones.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.370
Then, don't we just have to defeat them?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.130
Those Shingan guys defeated one the other day.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:20.880
I know. But that won't solve the real problem.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.260
Then, what should we do...?

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.840
I said so before, didn't I?

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:31.100
The only way to completely defeat
Dagger is through musical energy.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.560
The president of Unicorn Virtual Music, Dagger,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.110
has been one of the organizers
of this festival from the beginning.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:48.200
He planned to use this festival as a means
of furthering his own ambition from the start.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:53.910
Dagger's real goal is to
gather top musicians to himself.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.080
His targets are Shu☆zo from Trichronika,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.050
Darudayu from Tsurezurenaru Ayatsuri Mugenan,

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.630
and you, Cyan.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:12.350
His plan is to have Cyan join those
two to form Midi City's greatest band.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.100
That would be really bad, pyuru...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.900
The important part is what I'll tell you next.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.320
If our opponent is trying to
make his ambitions come true,

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.780
then we can use the
festival to defeat Dagger, too.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.360
Does that mean...?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:30.700
Yes. We will defeat
Dagger with your performance.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.410
Pyuru...

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.200
Can we...

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.960
...do that?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.790
There's no time to waste.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.170
For the sake of the music in this world,
for all the Myumons who love music—

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.510
You're the only ones who can do it.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:53.390
The song you wrote at training camp,
"Ryuusei Dreamline," has power.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.230
Dagger will probably also
prepare a new song for this festival.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:02.400
Don't yield to that song.
Please save this world with your performance.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:05.190
I'm sure you can do it.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.860
All right.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:07.900
Yeah.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.990
We'll try, pyuru.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.210
These are beautiful flowers.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:23.590
All are blooming in competition with each other.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.510
Yes, all the flowers...

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.340
...are very beautiful.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:33.810
Bands are the same. All compete with
each other to radiate their originality.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.930
That is what makes it interesting.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.980
No matter how beautiful and peerless the flower,

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:47.490
having only a single flower
in this world is too dreary.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.410
I would like your counsel
regarding Grateful King.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:57.370
Hm, is King still confined in the studio?

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:02.290
Yes. Dagger is using his
contract to force Grateful King

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.300
to write a new song for
the Grateful Rock Festival.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:09.840
Up until now, he has somehow
managed to stall for time...

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.180
...but that also seems to be at its limit.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:18.890
And, did you say her name was Cyan? That girl.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:23.400
Yes. There is reason for
Dagger to have his eye on her.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:27.320
Her Melodisian is evolving very quickly,

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:31.200
but it's hard to say if she
will be able to beat the song

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.360
of the one and only Grateful King in the end.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:38.870
So you would like me to lend you my strength?

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.080
Yes.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:51.970
I had simply wanted to allow myself
to go with the flow of this world...

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:59.430
...but I cannot overlook those who
want to defy the reason of the world.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:05.310
A, Un, follow me!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.400
Master, we will...

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.820
...stay by your side wherever you go!

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.490
Something is wrong.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.160
This was not how it was supposed to be.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:31.670
Hey, Grateful King.
Won't you tell me where I went wrong?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.480
This is...!

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:50.690
What?!

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.150
I'm sorry.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:56.030
But that's why I will be taking
a break from practice today.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.740
It's unusual for you to miss practice, Chuchu.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.830
Will it rain marshmallows next, pyuru?

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.410
Especially at such an important time.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:08.540
Oh my, I need a change of
pace sometimes, too, you know.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.340
Change of pace?

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.800
Well, I'll be going, then.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.690
You must be surprised that
I would contact you out of the blue.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:33.150
During the battle of the bands with
Criticrista the other day, you shone remarkably.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.660
I would like to meet you and speak
with you in person. How about it?

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.730
Miss Chuchu, we have been expecting you.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.460
It's so pretty. And fast.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.300
Completely different from our agency.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.260
Welcome to Unicorn Virtual Music.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:45.640
Your performance was wonderful
during the concert the other day.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:51.060
That's not all. You have more
ambition than anyone else in this world.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.310
Th-That's...

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:02.070
You want to shine more than anyone, don't you?

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.030
You want the audience
to look just at you, don't you?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.330
That's not...

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:11.420
Come work for me. Immediately.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.500
If you do that, you will be the
target of everyone's attention.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.880
It's such a waste, Chuchu.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.340
Why are you so hung up about that band?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.350
Plasmagica was just
supposed to be a stepping-stone.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.180
But—

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:34.440
Now, Chuchu, remember your ambition...

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.530
Here it is!

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:46.490
The first time I went
to an S-River concert hall,

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:52.000
I experienced a performance by The Great,
a band as great as their name implied.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:59.630
I remember the concert I watched
that day as clearly as if it were yesterday.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:04.680
- King! King! King!
- The wonderful performance that stole everyone's hearts and wouldn't let go.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:11.270
- King! King! King! King! King!
- To have so many people focusing their eyes on him.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:21.740
If I could perform like that,
then everyone will look at me, and only me.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.030
Before that, music was
something I enjoyed listening to.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:35.630
But ever since that day, I wanted people
to notice me because of my performance.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.710
Eventually, I saved up
my allowance to buy a guitar.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:47.430
It seemed easier to get noticed playing in
a band because it was showier than going solo.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.140
When I thought that—

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.770
This is who I am.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:56.730
You're the president of Banded
Rocking Records, Maple Arisugawa?

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:01.030
It was a minor label I had never heard of.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:05.110
But I thought of it as the
first step toward my ambition...

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.740
That's right. I can't let it end here...

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:13.830
Because the band was nothing
more than a stepping-stone for me.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.960
And at that time, I thought,

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:22.300
"If this girl joins our band, then
Plasmagica will definitely be noticed."

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:29.640
With that attention, everyone would focus
their eyes on me like they focused on King.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.810
When that happens,

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:37.270
I would be able to graduate from Plasmagica
and take off magnificently on my own.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:49.820
That's right. In order to make
my ambitions come true, I will do anything.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.460
Welcome, Chuchu.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.800
Huh? Chuchu?!

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.050
Dagger, what are you doing?!

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:10.430
Oh? It looks like you are
already resolved to do this.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:15.890
Yes. I have decided to quit Plasmagica.

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.690
Well said, Chuchu.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:23.110
Now, what will Cyan think about that?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.690
So that's how it is.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:29.450
You're trying to use Chuchu
to make Cyan despair.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:34.950
If Cyan's Melodisian, which has
evolved so much, became dark...

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.160
I wonder how much power it would have...

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.380
I cannot even begin to imagine.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.920
Damn it!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:48.260
Are you trying to possess
Strawberry Heart again?

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:50.010
How did you know about that?!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:54.060
Did you think that I had not noticed?

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.220
But you've just about reached your
limit with that, too, haven't you?

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:01.100
If you continue to do that,
won't you be in danger yourself?

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:05.520
Oh? I'm moved that you would worry about me.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.230
Don't think so highly of yourself.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:12.910
<i>You're</i> not the one I need.
I only need your song.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.410
Now, Chuchu. Go.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:21.040
Make your ambitions come
true by betraying your friends

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:24.040
and sending them to the depths of despair.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.380
Yes, sir.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.050
Chuchu! You can't go!

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:30.630
Howl as much as you want.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:33.590
There is nothing more you can do.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.860
This new snack is pretty good, pyuru.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:47.980
Yeah.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.400
Oh, welcome back, Chuchu.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:50.700
That was fast.

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:54.870
You've got a good nose, Chuchu.
We're just about to have snacks, pyuru!

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.790
Chuchu?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.080
I am quitting Plasmagica today.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.500
Um... pyuru?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.800
What are you saying, Chuchu?

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:11.840
This joke isn't funny.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.220
You're lying, aren't you?

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:19.140
Actually, I have decided
to join Unicorn Virtual Music.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.390
What?

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:25.480
My goal was always to have a solo career.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:29.780
Plasmagica was never more
than a stepping-stone to that end.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.860
No...

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.320
We must part ways, everyone.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.410
No! Don't let Chuchu leave!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.750
Moa, let me go.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.750
No, I won't, pyuru!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.050
Chuchu's been brainwashed by Dagger!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.590
What? She has?

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.680
Don't get in my way, you two!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.100
Chuchu!

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:08.020
Listen carefully! This is a
song you wrote for Plasmagica!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.940
What is this? Stop it!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:18.160
We're not rejecting your desire to
become a star with a solo career, pyuru!

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:29.170
But was Plasmagica really just a stepping-stone?

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.930
Chuchu, that's not true, is it?

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:56.950
Chuchu!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:15.210
To me... Plasmagica...

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:20.930
...wasn't just a stepping stone!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.150
I...

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:36.900
Dagger... Dagger used you...

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:44.200
He wanted to use you...
to make Cyan's Melodisian turn dark...

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.200
But, I'm glad.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:49.620
I...

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.880
I'm glad your brainwashing went away, pyuru!

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:56.590
It was kind of a lame shock
to be called a stepping-stone.

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.420
I'm sorry.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.470
Those were my true feelings.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:06.470
I'm really, really sorry!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:16.070
I really did think of
Plasmagica as a stepping-stone.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:24.370
Everything I did for the band up till now
was all to make my own ambitions come true.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:29.830
Having Cyan write a song, and suggesting
that we sing twin lead vocals together—

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:33.790
Everything was because I just wanted
Plasmagica to become more popular

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:40.760
so that I could get noticed...
It was all for myself!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.600
It was fine in the end, though!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:49.560
Huh?

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:53.560
Your ambitions helped Plasmagica, too, pyuru!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.360
Besides, if it was just the three of us,

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:58.980
we might not have been
able to keep this band going.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:02.200
We were able to make it
this far thanks to you, pyuru!

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.360
Yeah, that's right.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.870
Don't put it like that.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:10.160
It wouldn't be very interesting if we didn't
have at least one slightly evil character.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.420
She's right, pyuru!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.630
No matter what your ambitions are,

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.920
do you really want to
leave Plasmagica right now?

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:30.310
I will answer that plainly.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.770
I have no intention of doing that!

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:34.810
Yay!

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.440
Then, let's start practice!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.280
Okay, pyuru!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.700
Mr. Berry, thank you.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:53.000
Mr. Berry...?

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:03.130
<i>If you like it, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:06.010
<i>You can do it because you like it</i>

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:08.720
<i>The feeling that you like music</i>

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:12.100
<i>Can't be stopped by anyone</i>

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:20.520
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:22.740
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:26.280
<i>Running through my body</i>

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:28.820
<i>This electric thrill</i>

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:33.830
<i>Is this feeling curiosity?</i>

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:37.370
<i>Negativity is a decrescendo</i>

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:40.040
<i>Hope and expectations, a crescendo</i>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:45.590
<i>Show off our passion and</i>
<i>get god to be our ally, too</i>

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:51.100
<i>I wanna share with everyone and have a taste of</i>

00:22:51.310 --> 00:22:54.810
<i>Big!! Rocking!! Heart-throbbing!! Happiness!!!!</i>

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:58.850
<i>If it's you, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:01.860
<i>You can do it because it's you</i>

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:06.950
<i>Let's try performing these</i>
<i>dream-colored notes together</i>

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:10.160
<i>I want to tell you directly</i>

00:23:10.370 --> 00:23:12.990
<i>A life-sized, "heart-sized" heart</i>

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:15.870
<i>In order for it to reach you...</i>

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:19.210
<i>I will sing with all I have</i>

00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:21.960
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:23.920
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:27.510
Too bright! Oh, it's Shu☆zo!

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:30.300
I can only shine thanks to all my fans!

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:33.390
My brilliant singing voice reflects
off the mirrors of their hearts,

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:35.640
and that reflection makes it sparkle even more!

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:37.520
President Maple,
your reflection is extraordinary.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:39.690
Let's settle this on the tennis courts!
